<p>When magma moves underneath a volcano, it causes the surface of the volcano to change. This is known as deformation. Researchers recently calculated the amount of deformation occurring each month for five volcanoes in Latin America. Although Sierra Negra experienced a lot of deformation, its deformation rate was still lower than that of <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the statement?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f4035976-65ec-411d-af53-9095e54b5132","content":"<p>Alcedo.</p>"},{"id":"3017dce4-cea8-4d66-997d-0c6986a0781f","content":"<p>Pacaya.</p>"},{"id":"065f81a5-d457-41ac-82de-666f1227fc13","content":"<p>Fernandina.</p>"},{"id":"a14cad65-9b84-462c-ad34-c87d49051e15","content":"<p>Maule.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3017dce4-cea8-4d66-997d-0c6986a0781f"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. Pacaya had a deformation rate of almost 3.5 centimeters per month, while Sierra Negra had a deformation rate of less than 3 centimeters per month. Therefore, Sierra Negra&rsquo;s deformation rate was lower than Pacaya&rsquo;s. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Alcedo has a lower rate of deformation than Sierra Negra. Choice C is incorrect. Fernandina has a lower rate of deformation than Sierra Negra. Choice D is incorrect. Maule has a lower rate of deformation than Sierra Negra. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-QUA-E009$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$100d4e5e-196c-457d-a2f1-35ca44619988$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"89f71526","external_id":"d3e209e2-4be9-4b2a-8eeb-6c0b841d615f","vaultid":"9694c54d-1778-4733-af9c-afc4157fe39e","uId":"b7ffde45-80d0-4da1-aeb2-7b55e92e506f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"INI","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill_cd":"COE","skill_desc":"Command of Evidence","difficult